@201 = ~What do my eyes behold? By my beard! You possess the catalyst of Johrünbrumd, the masterpiece of Grolin Rockhands!~
@202 = ~If you can gather the components listed on this parchment, it would be my honor to complete the master's work.~
@203 = ~You have all the components required to forge Johrünbrumd, the master's final masterpiece. I can forge it for a mere 8,000 gold pieces.~
@204 = ~A pity. Well then, let's see if you've brought me anything else of interest...~
@208 = ~You know, when I forged Johrunbrumd from the plans left by Master Grolin Rockhands, it occurred to me that the Celestial Fury katana would complement the original design perfectly.~
@209 = ~If you could bring me that katana along with a pinch of fairy dust, I could combine the two weapons and make Johrünbrumd even more powerful.~
@2010 = ~You have Johrünbrumd, Celestial Fury, and the fairy dust. If it pleases you, I can reforge Johrünbrumd according to my own design. I ask only 6,000 gold pieces for the work.~
@2011 = ~But... can it be? Is that the Star of Kahor? The legendary blade forged from steel fallen from the heavens?~
@2012 = ~If you could find another metal that came from the stars, I could attempt to fuse the two together.~
@2013 = ~You have the Star of Kahor and another metal from the stars. If you wish, I can make the Star even more powerful. My fee is 3,000 gold pieces.~